[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table already shows a
second cause with no ticket, and a footnote about reports that do not fit either. Read report by
report, the ticket holds **three problems**. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other two keep coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} {filed} />

The counts above are computed from `reports-4471.json` at render time, with duplicate export rows
removed by id. If the desk merges more reports, the table follows.

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month first.** A day-first tenant books 7 April
and the invite says 4 July. Day and month swap, so it only happens when the day is 12 or less. Every
tenant on file writes the day first. This is what #4471 describes, and the queued fix is for this.

**`hint` — booking-v3's form tells people to type month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`, people type what it says, and the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. The report looks exactly like a parser report: a swapped day and month. It comes only through
the `form` channel of booking-v3 tenants. Fixing the parser does not touch it. Intake's tag does not
tell the two apart; it guesses from the browser, so go by tenant, form and channel
(`causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` does this).

**`one-day` — the date moves by one day, the month stays right.** Tuesday shows as Monday; a client
in Lisbon gets Tuesday and one in Toronto gets Monday for the same meeting; an invite arrives before
the booking; "every booking in June is one day off". That is a date shifted across a time zone or a
DST change, not a swapped day and month. #4471's table files these under `parser` by tenant and
footnotes them. The parser fix will not move them back.

## For the desk

- Do not close #4471 on the parser fix alone. Check the `hint` and `one-day` rows first.
- A swapped date from a booking-v3 tenant's form is `hint`, whatever intake tagged it.
- A date off by exactly one day is `one-day`. Do not merge it into a swap ticket because the subject
  says "wrong day": subjects match across all three problems.

